From 100a342ec1458cc674a511b719a3a99f79c45437 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dynamiteswag81 <318143412+dynamiteswag81@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:41:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] wasm: add WebAssembly architecture port

New arch/wasm: a !MMU, uniprocessor port where every task runs in its
own host worker (Web Worker) instance of the kernel module, all sharing
one linear memory. Context switches hand a baton between workers with
memory.atomic.wait/notify. Interrupts are delivered at irq-enable points.
User programs are PIE wasm modules loaded by binfmt_wasm.

Generic changes needed for a linker without linker scripts and a target
without return/label addresses:
 - sectionless initcalls (__start_/__stop_ per level)
 - switch dispatch for the BPF interpreter instead of computed goto
 - scheduler classes ordered by table instead of by address
 - _RET_IP_/_THIS_IP_ fallbacks, no asm EXPORT_SYMBOL tables
 - build: skip modpost, no built-in initramfs, CRLF-tolerant fixdep

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
